# What must never enter a build context.
#
# ★ THIS FILE DID NOT EXIST, AND EVERY IMAGE COPIED THE LOT ★
#
# All four Dockerfiles do `COPY . .` from the repo root. With no ignore list
# that is literally everything in the working tree, and two of those things are
# serious:
#
#   apps/api/.env      The Discord bot token, the OAuth client secret, the
#                      state secret, the token-encryption keyring and the
#                      database password — baked into an image layer, readable
#                      by anyone who can `docker save` or pull the image, and
#                      still there after a later layer deletes it.
#
#   node_modules/      Half a gigabyte of the BUILD MACHINE's dependencies,
#                      including native binaries compiled for the host. It also
#                      broke the build outright: pnpm tries to purge a modules
#                      directory it did not create and aborts without a TTY
#                      (ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY).
#
# The second is why this was found. The first is why it matters.

# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every shape, not just the one that exists today. `.env` alone would have
# missed `apps/api/.env`, which is the one that is actually on disk.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
**/secrets/

# ── dependencies and build output ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The image installs and builds from the lockfile itself, so anything already
# built here is at best redundant and at worst compiled for the wrong platform.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/companion/release
apps/companion/build

# ── version control and CI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.git` is often the largest single directory in the context and nothing in
# the image reads it.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── local noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode
.idea
.claude
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── things that describe the build rather than take part in it ───────────────
docs
infra/scripts
README.md

# ★ `ssot/` IS NOT IN THIS LIST, AND MUST NOT BE ★
#
# It looks like documentation and it is not: the promotion run READS
# `ssot/02-domain/rank-progression.yaml` at runtime to get the ladder
# (promotion-run.wiring.ts). Excluding it builds an image that passes every
# test, starts cleanly, and throws "rank-progression.yaml has no ladder
# section" on the 1st of the month at midnight — the one night nobody is
# watching. It was in this list for about a minute.
